Hyper-V privileged helper service (Windows host)

Usage:
  warden hyperv [command]

Available Commands:
  service     Manage the privileged Hyper-V helper service (LocalSystem)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for hyperv

Global Flags:
      --color string     color output (auto, always, never)
      --config string    config file to read, the only one that is (default: WARDEN_CONFIG, then ./warden.toml if it exists)
      --driver string    driver to run: container (default), qemu, vz, hyperv or firecracker, or the name or path of another driver binary
      --runtime string   container runtime (finch, docker, podman)
  -v, --verbose          verbose output

Use "warden hyperv [command] --help" for more information about a command.
